        pack              = 'Wings of the Goddess',
        rewards           = 'Cobra Staff',
        previous_quest    = 'Sins of the Mothers',
        next_quest        = 'Manifest Destiny',
        note              = ': You need to wait a game day after completing Sins of the Mothers before you can activate this quest. Zone into Windurst Waters (S) from West Sarutabaruta (S) for a cutscene. Collect the Magicite from the three present day beastmen strongholds again (these may be done in any order): Magicite Locations Davoi Make your way to Davoi. Head to (G-7) and click on the Wall of Dark Arts. Walk down the path into a large room and inspect the Magicite for the Key ItemShard of optistone. Beadeaux Enter Beadeaux from Pashhow Marshlands at (L-11). The fastest travel method is the Survival Guide warp to Beadeaux. Head back to the tunnel at (H-7) inside follow the left wall to zone into Qulun Dome. If you get a message that your silver bell, coruscant rosary, and black matinee necklace "glow faintly.", move closer to the door and try again until they "shine brightly!" and it opens. Examine the Magicite for the Key ItemShard of aurastone. Castle Oztroja Castle Oztroja is located at (L-8) in Meriphataud Mountains. The fastest travel method is the Survival Guide warp to Castle Oztroja. Enter and head to the door at (I-8). You will see a lever at either side of the door. One lever will open the door and the other will open a trap in the floor and cause you to fall into a pit. There is a very easy way to open this door. Stand between the two levers in front of the door. Trigger one of the levers and immediately run into the door. If done correctly, you should remain on the small edge in front of the door, even if the trapdoor opens. If that happens, just wait until it\'s closed again and try again with the other lever. On the second floor, head to (G-7) where you will exit into a courtyard. On this map, head north (without falling off) to a the corridor leading into the next map at (I-7). Here follow the right wall until you reach a door at (H-9). The mobs in this area are much higher level than the ones previously encountered. At the door light the torch and you will be taken through. Head South and take a right to another door. Click on the brass door to open it. The zone is just ahead. Inside you will be in an area with no mobs. Examine the Magicite for the Key ItemShard of orastone. Once you have all three Magicite, return to Windurst Waters (S) and speak to Velda-Galda (K-9) for a cutscene. Zone into West Sarutabaruta (S) from Windurst Waters (S) for another cutscene. Examine the Windurstian Bulwark (J-8), located just ahead for a cutscene. Examine the Windurstian Bulwark to start a fight. This fight begins immediately and takes place on the field. Buff before examining. The time limit for this fight is 30 minutes and you are allowed to bring a full alliance of 18 people to this fight. Only the person initiating this fight needs to have the quest active. Killing the Tiny Lycopodiums before the fight makes targetting easier as they tend to follow you around. Clearing the Lycopodiums out with Area of Effect damage is recommended. Four waves of monsters will spawn and attempt to destroy the 3 Magical Barriers. Wave one is a group of 6 Yagudos: Yagudo Parivirs. Wave two is a group of 3 Taurus: Giganotaurs. Wave three is a group of 6 Demons Black Mages: Kindred Incantor. Wave four is a group of 3 Ahrimans: Blurry Eyes. Both Romaa Mihgo and at least one of the three Protective Wards must be kept alive. The Protective Wards cannot be Cured and they also take damage from AoE\'s. Curing Waltz can be used to heal the Protective Wards. If you fail the fight, you can zone and reinspect the Windurstian Bulwark to try again. Once you have finished the fight, before zoning examine the Windurstian Bulwark again for a long cutscene or you\'ll have to do the fight again. Zone into Windurst Waters (S) for the final cutscene and your reward. If you are working on missions then return to Fate in Haze.',
        walkthrough       = {

            { 'Wait a game day after completing Sins of the Mothers before activating this quest.' },
            { 'Zone into Windurst Waters (S) from West Sarutabaruta (S) for a cutscene.' },
            { '── Collect Magicite from the three present-day beastman strongholds (any order) ──' },
            { 'Davoi — head to (G-7), click the Wall of Dark Arts, walk down into a large room and inspect the Magicite for Key Item Shard of optistone.' },
            { 'Beadeaux — enter from Pashhow Marshlands at (L-11), then head back to the tunnel at (H-7) and follow the left wall to zone into Qulun Dome; examine the Magicite for Key Item Shard of aurastone.', sub = {
                { 'Fastest travel: Survival Guide warp to Beadeaux.' },
                { 'If the silver bell, coruscant rosary, and black matinee necklace "glow faintly", move closer to the door and try again until they "shine brightly!" and open it.' },
            } },
            { 'Castle Oztroja — located at (L-8) in Meriphataud Mountains; enter and reach the Magicite for Key Item Shard of orastone.', sub = {
                { 'Fastest travel: Survival Guide warp to Castle Oztroja.' },
                { 'At the door at (I-8), stand between the two levers; trigger one and immediately run into the door to remain on the small edge. If the trapdoor opens, wait and try the other lever.' },
                { 'On the second floor head to (G-7) to exit into a courtyard; head north (without falling) to the corridor at (I-7).' },
                { 'Follow the right wall to a door at (H-9); mobs here are much higher level than before.' },
                { 'Light the torch at the door, head south, take a right, open the brass door, then zone in. Examine the Magicite for Key Item Shard of orastone.' },
            } },
            { 'Return to Windurst Waters (S) and speak to Velda-Galda at (K-9) for a cutscene.' },
            { 'Zone into West Sarutabaruta (S) from Windurst Waters (S) for another cutscene.' },
            { 'Examine the Windurstian Bulwark at (J-8) for a cutscene.' },
            { 'Examine the Windurstian Bulwark again to start a field fight.', sub = {
                { 'Fight starts immediately; buff before examining. Time limit 30 minutes, full alliance of 18 allowed.' },
                { 'Only the initiator needs the quest active.' },
                { 'Kill the Tiny Lycopodiums first for easier targeting; AoE damage recommended.' },
                { 'Four waves spawn: 6x Yagudo Parivirs, 3x Giganotaurs (Taurus), 6x Kindred Incantor (Demon BLM), 3x Blurry Eyes (Ahriman).' },
                { 'Romaa Mihgo and at least one of the three Protective Wards must survive; Wards cannot be Cured and take AoE damage, but Curing Waltz works on them.' },
                { 'If you fail, zone and re-inspect the Windurstian Bulwark to try again.' },
            } },
            { 'After winning, examine the Windurstian Bulwark again before zoning for a long cutscene, or you\'ll have to redo the fight.' },
            { 'Zone into Windurst Waters (S) for the final cutscene and your reward.' },
            { 'If working on missions, return to Fate in Haze.' },
        },
    },
    ['In a Haze of Glory'] = {
        title             = 'In a Haze of Glory',
        starting_npc      = 'Diordinne, Garlaige Citadel (S)',
        subtitle          = 'None',
        repeatable        = 'No',
        description       = 'Despite heightened security, the Garlaige Citadel has been infiltrated by an unseen enemy who is emitting poisonous gas with brutal results. Amidst the confusion, zealous new captain, Rahal, has ventured off on his own. Find him and ensure he does not come to harm.',
        required_fame     = 'Unknown',
        level_restriction = 'None',
        pack              = 'Wings of the Goddess',
        rewards           = 'Fullmetal Bullet',
        previous_quest    = 'Perils of the Griffon',
        next_quest        = 'The Price of Valor',
        note              = 'If you fail the BC, you will need to wait a game day to re-acquire the Key Item Number eight shelter key. You must return and speak with Diordinne to begin the game day wait for the KI. Head back to Southern San d\'Oria (S) and speak to Rholont (E-7) during nighttime hours (18:00 to 0:00 game time) to complete the quest and receive your reward. Maps Garlaige Citadel (S) Map 1 Garlaige Citadel (S) Map 1 Garlaige Citadel (S) Map 2 Garlaige Citadel (S) Map 2 Ghoyu\'s Reverie Map 15 Ghoyu\'s Reverie Map 15',
        walkthrough       = {

            { 'Speak to Diordinne at (I-6) on the first map of Garlaige Citadel (S) to begin the quest and receive Key Item Number eight shelter key.' },
            { 'Head east into the second map to (H-9) and examine the Wooden Crates.', sub = {
                { 'Party leader must examine; buffs wear on entry.' },
            } },
            { 'Defeat the Orcish Turret in Ghoyu\'s Reverie within 30 minutes.', sub = {
                { 'On Map 15 (spawn map), travel south to around (H-10) along the western walls to find the Turret.' },
                { 'Beware Goblin Effluvial Grenade — Noxious Spray causes heavy poison.' },
                { 'Effluvial Flasks have ~150 HP and do not need to be destroyed.' },
                { 'Other Orcs and Goblins (~1500 HP) do not need to be killed but may get in the way.' },
            } },
            { 'Defeating the Orcish Turret transports you out immediately for a cutscene.', sub = {
                { 'If you fail the BC, wait a game day and speak to Diordinne again to re-acquire Key Item Number eight shelter key.' },
            } },
            { 'Return to Southern San d\'Oria (S) and speak to Rholont at (E-7) during nighttime hours (18:00 to 0:00 game time) to complete the quest and receive your reward.' },
            { '── Maps ──' },
        },
        notes             = {

            { 'Trivial at 99.' },
            { 'Dancer sub with Healing Waltz handles the Noxious Spray easily.' },
            { 'SMN75 + PLD75/DNC took 20 minutes easily.' },
        },
    },
    ['Knot Quite There'] = {
